Worker change for the larger model's weights as an external data file (ci/lab/patches/worker-external-data.patch)

Against vendor/rec-worker.js on main at build 8 (8037aec). Apply with: git apply ci/lab/patches/worker-external-data.patch
It needs a new file: the graph and weights published on pub/model-bioclip2-l14-b (ci/lab/mem_pub.sh), and a change in
the page (src/cam.rec.js) that is not in this patch: fetch vision.graph.onnx and the parts of vision.weights.bin, check
them against parts.json, and send init with model = the graph's bytes, weights = the joined weights, weightsName =
'vision.weights.bin' (transfer both buffers). With no m.weights the worker behaves exactly as before.

Measured (onnxruntime-web 1.30.0 WASM, one thread; tools/lab/mem_node.mjs in Node 22 on GitHub ubuntu-latest machines;
tables by tools/lab/mem_table.py from runs/lab/32-mem-base and runs/lab/33-mem-b on the ci branch):
  shipped file (vision.int8.onnx, 309,812,341 bytes), worker's options:  WASM heap 819.4 MiB; peak resident 1249 MiB
    while the session is created, 1167 MiB during photos 1 and 10 with the file's bytes let go
  external data (vision.graph.onnx 2,175,801 bytes + vision.weights.bin 307,658,752 bytes), same options: WASM heap
    429.0 MiB (-47.6%); peak resident 814 MiB while the session is created, 630 and 632 MiB during photos 1 and 10
    with the bytes let go
  vectors of 24 test photos: identical to the shipped file's (largest absolute difference 0.0; cosine 1.0000000)
  seconds a photo: 2.79 (shipped, run 32 machine) and 4.85 (external, run 33 machine); these were different machines,
    and the shipped file through the page's worker in Chromium on the run 33 machine took 4.39 s a photo

